{"path":"ranges/take_while_view/end","title":"std::ranges::take_while_view<V,Pred>::end","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::take_while_view&lt;V,Pred&gt;::</span>end","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view/end","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Returns a sentinel representing the end of the view.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> end<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> requires <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*simple-view*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> end<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> requires<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><span class=\"kw2916\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirect_unary_predicate\"><span class=\"kw3152\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirect_unary_predicate</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Pred, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view/sentinel\">sentinel</a> representing the end of the view.\n</p><p>Let <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view#Data_members\"><code><i>base_</i></code></a> denote the underlying view.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Effectively returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*sentinel*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw2\">false</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/end\"><span class=\"kw2902\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">end</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/addressof\"><span class=\"kw761\">std::<span class=\"me2\">addressof</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pred<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Effectively returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*sentinel*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw2\">true</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/end\"><span class=\"kw2902\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">end</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/addressof\"><span class=\"kw761\">std::<span class=\"me2\">addressof</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pred<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>Overload <span class=\"t-v\">(1)</span> does not participate in overload resolution if <code>V</code> is a <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges#Helper_concepts\">simple view</a> (that is, if <code>V</code> and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V</span> are views with the same iterator and sentinel types).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view/sentinel\">sentinel</a> representing the end of the view.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3450\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3450</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++20\n</td>\n<td>the <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> overload might return a sentinel non-comparable to the iterator\n</td>\n<td>constrained\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view/begin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>begin</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an iterator to the beginning <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view/sentinel/operator_cmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator==</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   compares a sentinel with an iterator returned from <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/take_while_view/begin\"><code>take_while_view::begin</code></a>  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/take_while_view","title":"std::ranges::views::take_while, std::ranges::take_while_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::take_while_view<V,Pred>::end","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Returns a sentinel representing the end of the view."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A sentinel representing the end of the view."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"begin","note":"returns an iterator to the beginning"},{"label":"operator==","note":"compares a sentinel with an iterator returned from take_while_view::begin"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":158,"codeBlockCount":0}
